---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Product roadmap"
  description="The verified Veasel Code foundation and the work ahead for a capable, safe V-native coding agent."
>
  <section class="doc-page">
    <p class="kicker">THE BUILD / WHAT’S NEXT</p>
    <h1>
      Make every step
      <br />
      <em>earn its place.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The roadmap grows from a working vertical slice. Each capability is
      described as available only after its runtime, user experience, and tests
      are in place.
    </p>
    <div class="roadmap-list">
      <article class="roadmap-item roadmap-done">
        <span class="roadmap-status">WORKING FOUNDATION</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Local sessions</h2>
          <p>
            V HTTP API, SQLite chat history, replayable SSE events, and an
            OpenTUI session client.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="roadmap-symbol" aria-label="Complete">
          ✓
        </span>
      </article>
      <article class="roadmap-item roadmap-done">
        <span class="roadmap-status">WORKING FOUNDATION</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Multiple provider families</h2>
          <p>
            Streaming chat across OpenAI-compatible APIs, OpenAI and Meta
            Responses, Anthropic, and Gemini, with persisted assistant events.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="roadmap-symbol" aria-label="Complete">
          ✓
        </span>
      </article>
      <article class="roadmap-item roadmap-done">
        <span class="roadmap-status">WORKING FOUNDATION</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Read-only workspace tools</h2>
          <p>
            Provider-native tool calls for bounded listing, UTF-8 reads, and
            literal search within the session’s canonical workspace root.
            Requested excerpts are sent to the configured provider.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="roadmap-symbol" aria-label="Complete">
          ✓
        </span>
      </article>
      <article class="roadmap-item roadmap-done">
        <span class="roadmap-status">WORKING FOUNDATION</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Local workspace API</h2>
          <p>
            Direct session-scoped file listing, reads, and literal search with
            path containment and symlink-safe traversal.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="roadmap-symbol" aria-label="Complete">
          ✓
        </span>
      </article>
      <article class="roadmap-item roadmap-done">
        <span class="roadmap-status">WORKING FOUNDATION</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Review-gated file edits</h2>
          <p>
            Propose bounded single-file replacements, inspect persisted diffs,
            and explicitly approve or reject changes in the TUI. Stale files are
            rejected; interrupted writes are not replayed.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="roadmap-symbol" aria-label="Complete">
          ✓
        </span>
      </article>
      <article class="roadmap-item roadmap-done">
        <span class="roadmap-status">WORKING FOUNDATION</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Approved shell commands</h2>
          <p>
            Store each proposed command for review. The TUI exposes its exact
            text, working directory, and timeout before explicit approval;
            execution is bounded and never replayed after interruption. Commands
            still run with the server user's permissions and without an OS
            sandbox.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="roadmap-symbol" aria-label="Complete">
          ✓
        </span>
      </article>
      <article class="roadmap-item roadmap-done">
        <span class="roadmap-status">WORKING FOUNDATION</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Configured MCP and OAuth PKCE</h2>
          <p>
            User/project servers, portable <code>.mcp.json</code> import, named
            HTTP credentials, and authorization-code + PKCE authorize/complete
            with optional loopback <code>--listen</code> (prints the URL; no
            automatic browser launch). Per-session trust and per-call approval
            still gate every tool effect.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="roadmap-symbol" aria-label="Complete">
          ✓
        </span>
      </article>
      <article class="roadmap-item roadmap-active">
        <span class="roadmap-status">IN DEVELOPMENT</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Reliable cancellation</h2>
          <p>
            Escape and API cancellation stop queued work and signal active
            provider requests. A request cancelled before its first response
            chunk still waits for the bounded transport cleanup timeout. MCP
            transports emit best-effort <code>notifications/cancelled</code> for
            in-flight requests.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="roadmap-symbol" aria-label="In progress">
          ◌
        </span>
      </article>
      <article class="roadmap-item roadmap-active">
        <span class="roadmap-status">IN DEVELOPMENT</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Agent Plugins compatibility</h2>
          <p>
            Local Skills, plugin component toggles, and trusted stdio or
            Streamable HTTP MCP servers are experimental and available per
            session. Every MCP tool call still pauses for argument review and
            one-time approval. Managed installation, automatic OAuth browser
            launch, additional conformance fixtures, and the full Agent Plugins
            v1.0.0 evidence gate remain in progress.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="roadmap-symbol" aria-label="In progress">
          ◌
        </span>
      </article>
      <article class="roadmap-item roadmap-active">
        <span class="roadmap-status">IN DEVELOPMENT</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Durable work</h2>
          <p>
            Async session turns persist status before acceptance, resume queued{" "}
            <code>Prefer: respond-async</code> work after restart (bounded per
            session; autonomous resume requires{" "}
            <code>VEASEL_ALLOW_AUTONOMOUS_EXECUTION=1</code>), and can be
            queried after reconnect. Mid-flight work interrupted by a restart is
            classified as <code>uncertain</code> and never replayed. Operation
            history management and retention policy remain ahead.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="roadmap-symbol" aria-label="In progress">
          ◌
        </span>
      </article>
      <article class="roadmap-item roadmap-next">
        <span class="roadmap-status">PLANNED</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Production distribution</h2>
          <p>
            Linux, macOS, and Windows preview archives are published with
            checksums. Code signing, native installers, broader accessibility,
            measured performance baselines, and stable releases remain ahead.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="roadmap-symbol" aria-label="Planned">
          ·
        </span>
      </article>
    </div>
    <aside class="callout">
      <strong>Product status can change.</strong> The repository’s
      implementation plan and CI results are the source of truth for current
      engineering progress.
    </aside>
    <p class="doc-next">
      <a
        class="text-link"
        href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md"
      >
        See the implementation plan <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/`}>
        Browse the full field guide <span aria-hidden="true">↑</span>
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
